  "notes": {
    "debriefQuestions": [],
    "limitations": [
      "Simulated respondents: the seeded demo run (scripts/results/seed-demo.mjs) walked the respondent flow, not a fielded panel. Every figure on this wave exercises the pipeline; none is a measurement.",
      "No multiplicity adjustment is applied across subgroups."
    ],
    "methodology": [
      "Counted: 2464 complete records, the latest per panel id, env development. Not counted: 0 complete(s) from another env, 0 earlier duplicate(s), 0 with an arm outside the test, 0 screenout(s); 14 start record(s) seen.",
      "Raked to education, party, vote2024 in 4 iterations (largest remaining gap 9.7e-9); weights normalized to mean 1, range 0.27899999999999997 to 5.004, capped at 5 (23 capped). Targets: Massachusetts general adults (18+), derived from the audience store by scripts/results/targets.mjs.",
      "Weighting target, education (as raked): hs-or-less 31.2%, some-college 21.5%, bachelors-plus 47.3%. American Community Survey 5-year estimates (U.S. Census Bureau); education_4 @25, count; period 2020-01-01 to 2024-12-31; universe population 25+; proxy: population 25+; derivation audience-store. B15003 covers ages 25 and over; the store has no 18–24 education for the state, so the 25+ distribution stands in for adults 18+ and likely overstates bachelor's-or-higher for them.",
      "Weighting target, party (as raked): democrat 37.3%, republican 14.6%, independent-other 48.2%. Cooperative Election Study common content 2020, 2022, 2024 (Harvard University); pid3 @25, 2024, pct (commonweight); period 2024-01-01 to 2024-12-31; universe adults 18+ (CES state respondents, commonweight); derivation audience-store. Party identification, a survey estimate: n 1119, margin of error up to ±4 points. The printed shares sum to 100.1 and are renormalized to 100. Identification, not enrollment: the state's party enrollment measures registration, a different construct on a different universe. 2024 is used to match the 2024 vote target (--party-year picks another); the store also holds 2023 (n 383, ±5) and 2025 (n 272, ±6.3).",
      "Weighting target, vote2024 (as raked): democrat 37.4%, republican 22.0%, did-not-vote 38.2%, other 2.4%. Official ballot-measure results (state election offices); American Community Survey 5-year estimates (U.S. Census Bureau); presidential_vote @25, 2024, count; ACS age_bucket @25 (adults 18+); period 2024-11-05 to 2024-11-05; universe adults 18+; derivation audience-store. 3,512,930 ballots cast ÷ 5,679,875 adults 18+; \"Did not vote\" is the adults who cast no ballot (38.15%), non-citizen adults included. Blank presidential lines (a ballot cast, no presidential choice) count with \"other\" under the pax-entry map. Respondents over-report voting, so raking to the true non-vote share up-weights the non-voters a panel yields.",
      "Declared but not asked by this test, so not raked: age, gender, race.",
      "Levels are weighted percentages. Lifts are arm level minus placebo level, in points, with a margin of 1.645 standard errors. Each comparison is a two-sided two-proportion z-test with Kish effective sample sizes; detectable means p < 0.1 and at least 50 actual respondents in both groups."
    ],
    "noEffectMeaning": "Inconclusive means the comparison did not meet the criterion; it is not evidence of zero effect.",
    "notSupported": [
      "Comparisons between video arms: each arm is tested only against the placebo.",
      "A verdict from any arm or subgroup with fewer than 50 actual respondents: those comparisons are inconclusive by rule."
    ],
    "supported": [
      "Randomized comparison of each video arm with the placebo arm on stated ballot choice and comprehension."
    ]
  },
